# .dockerignore (2026-09-14) - keeps the build context small and keeps secrets
# out of the image. Docker sends the ENTIRE context to the daemon before the
# first instruction runs, so every entry here is also a build-speed fix.
#
# The single most important lines are `.secrets` and `demo`:
#   - `.secrets/` holds the machine-local dev env file (DB password, Gmail app
#     password, key-ring path). It must never enter an image layer.
#   - `demo/` is ~450 MB of reference repositories (ADR 0012) that no
#     application file imports from. Shipping it would dominate the context.

# Dependencies - reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output - the image builds its own; a stale host dist must never win
dist
**/dist
**/.next
website/out
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets - never in an image layer
.secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Reference repos (ADR 0012) - imported by nothing under app/ admin/ website/
# packages/ db/ scripts/; ~450 MB
demo

# Project memory, agent config and docs - not needed to build or run
.memory
.claude
docs
plan
*.md
!db/migrations/README.md

# Local runtime state
.data
coverage
**/coverage
.vscode
.idea

# Tests and fixtures - the image runs the gate's OUTPUT, never the gate
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__tests__
**/__test-support__
**/test/fixtures
